# Summary of the root cause:
The cache key does not include the default locale used when locale parameter is null, which leads to returning formatters cached under the wrong key when default locale changes.

# This causes the failure observed in the test test_changeDefault_Locale_DateInstance where formatters for previous default locales are returned incorrectly after changing default locale.

# Suggest fixing the cache key to include default locale when locale parameter is null to avoid collisions.
Diagnosis:
The failure in the test method test_changeDefault_Locale_DateInstance is caused by the caching mechanism of FastDateFormat.getDateInstance(int, TimeZone, Locale) which uses a cache key derived from the style, timezone, and locale. However, when the locale parameter is null, the method uses Locale.getDefault() internally to create the formatter instance, but the default locale is not included as part of the cache key (because locale is null). This means that the cached formatter is keyed solely on style and possibly timezone, but not on the actual default locale used at the time of formatter creation.

When the default Locale is changed after caching a formatter created with a prior default locale (as in the test), further calls to getDateInstance(int) (which uses null locale) will reuse the cached formatter keyed without the current default locale included. Consequently, formatters with a stale or incorrect locale are returned, leading to the test failure where format instances do not reflect the current default Locale.

The root cause is thus that the cache key used when locale is null omits the actual default locale, violating the assumption that Locale.getDefault() does not change. This causes cache collisions and incorrect locale being applied after default locale changes.

The fix should involve including the effective locale used (i.e., Locale.getDefault() when locale param is null) as part of the cache key to avoid key collisions and ensure cached instances are properly distinguished by their locale.

